  "title": "Crack the code",
  "format": "build",
  "skills": [
    "logic.comparator",
    "logic.and-tree"
  ],
  "brief": {
    "story": "The workshop door lock opens only for the code 1010 on four switches (D3 D2 D1 D0). D3 and D1 must be on, D2 and D0 off: the off ones go through inverters (IC1) before the AND gates (IC2). The inverted bits aren’t wired into their AND gate.",
    "goal": "Wire NOT D0 and NOT D2 into IC2’s gate 2 so OPEN lights only for D3 D2 D1 D0 = 1 0 1 0.",
    "datasheet": {
      "title": "Code lock 1010",
      "rows": [
        [
          "IC1 74HC04",
          "NOT D0 → column 4 · NOT D2 → column 6"
        ],
        [
          "IC2 gate 1",
          "D3 · D1 (done)"
        ],
        [
          "IC2 gate 2",
          "pins 4, 5 = columns 20, 21"
        ],
        [
          "IC2 gate 3",
          "gate 1 · gate 2 → OPEN"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "hints": [
    "The lock is one big AND of four conditions: D3, NOT D2, D1, NOT D0. ANDs combine two at a time, so it takes three.",
    "Gate 2 of IC2 should get the two inverted bits: pin 4 is column 20, pin 5 is column 21. NOT D0 comes out of IC1 on column 4, NOT D2 on column 6.",
    "Column 4 → column 20, and column 6 → column 21."
  ],
